WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.722 --> 00:00:04.292
(dramatic orchestral music)

00:00:12.752 --> 00:00:13.727
- Monster headaches.

00:00:13.727 --> 00:00:14.633
- I'm so tired.

00:00:14.633 --> 00:00:15.376
- Lashing out.

00:00:15.376 --> 00:00:16.490
- [Woman in Gray] We want fucking water!

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:17.605
- Stop torturing me.

00:00:17.605 --> 00:00:18.882
- There's a psychological component.

00:00:18.882 --> 00:00:21.273
- I might die doing this. I
literally might die doing this.

00:00:21.273 --> 00:00:23.085
(woman screaming)

00:00:23.085 --> 00:00:25.656
(dramatic music crescendos)

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:32.070
- Coffee is life. Life
is coffee. (sips coffee)

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:33.812
- Like, on a normal day, I'm dehydrated.

00:00:33.812 --> 00:00:35.553
I'm probably dehydrated right now.

00:00:35.553 --> 00:00:38.130
- I don't know how to
watch Netflix without wine.

00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:41.195
- I'm addicted to coffee.
I love soda on the weekend.

00:00:41.195 --> 00:00:43.424
- I really hope to not be
dehydrated all the time.

00:00:43.424 --> 00:00:46.513
- I'd like to know what it
feels like to feel healthy.

00:00:46.513 --> 00:00:48.742
- I wanna be not addicted to caffeine.

00:00:48.742 --> 00:00:50.901
- I feel really sluggish in
the afternoons around 2 or 3,

00:00:50.901 --> 00:00:54.105
and I'm hoping that maybe
if I just go all water

00:00:54.105 --> 00:00:55.707
I'll have some more energy.

00:00:55.707 --> 00:00:58.517
- I can do this, 100%. (laughs)

00:00:58.517 --> 00:00:59.678
- Good morning, everybody.

00:00:59.678 --> 00:01:01.744
So, got my water, I'm ready to do this,

00:01:01.744 --> 00:01:03.880
I'm feelin' pretty good.

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:06.434
Actually, I'm pretty
excited. Let's do this!

00:01:06.434 --> 00:01:08.199
Healthy living: day one.

00:01:08.199 --> 00:01:09.824
It's day three. I feel
like I'm dying right now.

00:01:09.824 --> 00:01:11.984
Can I chew, like, coffee
beans for caffeine?

00:01:11.984 --> 00:01:15.234
- I went into this really
confident, but this is actually

00:01:15.234 --> 00:01:17.022
one of the hardest things I've ever done.

00:01:17.022 --> 00:01:20.552
I'm so tired. And all I
wanna do is drink coffee.

00:01:20.552 --> 00:01:22.014
- I have had a ton of withdrawal.

00:01:22.014 --> 00:01:23.152
I just feel terrible.

00:01:23.152 --> 00:01:24.104
- Monster headaches,

00:01:24.104 --> 00:01:26.751
lashing out at other people for no reason.

00:01:26.751 --> 00:01:28.562
- To me, I feel like this was
probably the toughest week.

00:01:28.562 --> 00:01:29.700
Cause it was the change.

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:32.997
I feel like now I'm sorta
getting used to not having tea.

00:01:32.997 --> 00:01:34.692
But the biggest bummer,
I think, was socializing.

00:01:34.692 --> 00:01:37.966
- [Voiceover] David. How's
that water thing coming, buddy?

00:01:37.966 --> 00:01:40.241
- The water thing is just great,

00:01:40.241 --> 00:01:43.933
and I was just getting
some water right now.

00:01:43.933 --> 00:01:45.233
- Which water were you gonna get in there?

00:01:45.233 --> 00:01:47.416
- And don't you guys
have jobs or something?

00:01:47.416 --> 00:01:49.691
Don't you have jobs? Get to your jobs.

00:01:49.691 --> 00:01:54.382
- Eating and drinking are
so tied to my social life.

00:01:54.382 --> 00:01:58.282
It's difficult to be at
breakfast and just drinking water

00:01:58.282 --> 00:02:00.070
and everyone else is drinking, like,

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:03.112
a coffee or some orange juice.

00:02:03.112 --> 00:02:05.782
- This challenge is the
worst possible thing.

00:02:05.782 --> 00:02:07.245
I've gained weight.

00:02:07.245 --> 00:02:09.172
- The fact that I'm drinking so much water

00:02:09.172 --> 00:02:12.766
makes me feel entitled to
make choices like nachos.

00:02:12.766 --> 00:02:15.020
I guess when I came into
this I was kinda hoping

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:16.388
that I would notice more energy,

00:02:16.388 --> 00:02:19.778
or notice something significant
about the way I feel change

00:02:19.778 --> 00:02:21.612
and that hasn't happened.

00:02:21.612 --> 00:02:24.700
- I also haven't been super
good about not drinking alcohol.

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:28.439
I just wanna have fun on a
Friday after the difficult week

00:02:28.439 --> 00:02:30.157
so I've had a few drinks.
(buzzer)

00:02:30.157 --> 00:02:32.502
and then I went to karaoke and

00:02:32.502 --> 00:02:34.387
(buzzer)
drank a lot. (laughs)

00:02:35.417 --> 00:02:38.332
(bouncy pop music)

00:02:41.624 --> 00:02:42.997
- So we're gonna play some kind of

00:02:42.997 --> 00:02:45.296
weird mash-up of Capture the Flag and tag?

00:02:47.506 --> 00:02:49.134
(woman screaming and laughing)

00:02:54.056 --> 00:02:55.704
- I feel okay, I feel pretty fine.

00:02:55.704 --> 00:02:59.326
I'm not too tired, so maybe I have been

00:02:59.326 --> 00:03:02.159
a lot more hydrated
these past three weeks.

00:03:02.159 --> 00:03:04.388
- Since I've started, the only
water thing I have noticed:

00:03:04.388 --> 00:03:07.825
the wall I hit at 3 or 4
pm has kind of gone away.

00:03:07.825 --> 00:03:09.566
- I've been managing my sleep better,

00:03:09.566 --> 00:03:12.492
so I force myself to go
to bed at a certain time

00:03:12.492 --> 00:03:14.953
if I know that the next
day I have to get up early.

00:03:14.953 --> 00:03:18.273
Cause usually I'll just use
coffee to cover all that up.

00:03:18.273 --> 00:03:20.850
- I also didn't realize
just how often in my life

00:03:20.850 --> 00:03:24.496
alcohol is just around, and
more often than not, free.

00:03:24.496 --> 00:03:26.052
In this past week I was
at three different parties

00:03:26.052 --> 00:03:28.977
where people were offering
me lots of free alcohol.

00:03:28.977 --> 00:03:30.370
Stop torturing me.

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:32.785
- This is way harder than I
thought it was going to be.

00:03:32.785 --> 00:03:35.455
This is just, this has been the worst.

00:03:35.775 --> 00:03:39.299
(dramatic orchestral music)

00:03:39.728 --> 00:03:43.234
- I'm about to explode
with happiness. Oh my gosh!

00:03:43.754 --> 00:03:45.773
(people sipping drinks)

00:03:45.904 --> 00:03:47.552
- It's been a long time.
(Steven sighs)

00:03:47.552 --> 00:03:49.085
- This is great.

00:03:49.085 --> 00:03:52.150
It is before 11:30 in the morning.

00:03:52.150 --> 00:03:55.540
- It's one week out and I feel
tired, still, all the time.

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:58.410
I feel like coffee should
really affect me now,

00:03:58.410 --> 00:04:00.601
but I feel like now I'm
just desensitized to it.

00:04:00.601 --> 00:04:02.481
- Doing this life change was really good

00:04:02.481 --> 00:04:05.430
because now any future
life changes I wanna make

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:06.730
I'm a little more prepared for.

00:04:06.730 --> 00:04:08.727
- My base lesson is that water should be

00:04:08.727 --> 00:04:10.562
what you drink as a baseline.

00:04:10.562 --> 00:04:13.510
- I can't tolerate coffee anymore.

00:04:13.510 --> 00:04:16.575
Which is so sad and so difficult.

00:04:16.575 --> 00:04:18.177
You're forcing me to be hydrated

00:04:18.177 --> 00:04:20.778
and not have an excessive
amount of caffeine.

00:04:20.778 --> 00:04:23.187
You...
You messed with my life.

00:04:25.337 --> 00:04:26.797
(laughing) You've changed my life.

00:04:32.132 --> 00:04:33.567
(bell tone)

